krdp 6.6.7: extended security off, one line of krdp 6.8's "Fix
authentication with FreeRDP 3.32" (upstream f868133, cherry-picked to
Plasma/6.8 as 31824f9). FreeRDP 3.32 enables extended security by
default, which selects PROTOCOL_HYBRID_EX whatever krdp asked for, and
logins fail. 6.6.7 offers TLS security only and checks the name and
password itself once the client is connected; the rest of that fix
(NLA against a SAM file when PAM isn't in use) is not taken here. On
the FreeRDP SteamOS ships today (3.23 on 0.5.11) the setting is
already off and this changes nothing; it is here for the update that
brings 3.32, and is untested against one.

--- a/src/RdpConnection.cpp
+++ b/src/RdpConnection.cpp
@@ -354,6 +354,7 @@
     freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_RdpSecurity, false);
     freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_TlsSecurity, true);
     freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_NlaSecurity, false);
+    freerdp_settings_set_bool(settings, FreeRDP_ExtSecurity, false);
 
     freerdp_settings_set_uint32(settings, FreeRDP_OsMajorType, OSMAJORTYPE_UNIX);
     // PSEUDO_XSERVER is apparently required for things to work properly.
